corrected:       server.conf [sslConfig] sslVersionsForClient matches (^|,)\s*tls1\.2\s*(,|$) -> server.conf [sslConfig] sslVersionsForClient matches ^[[:space:]]*(tls1\.2|tls1\.3)([[:space:]]*,[[:space:]]*(tls1\.2|tls1\.3))*[[:space:]]*$
vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] sslVersions https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/secure-splunk-platform-communications-with-transport-layer-security-certificates/configure-tls-protocol-version-support-for-secure-connections-between-splunk-platform-instances
vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] sslVersionsForClient https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/secure-splunk-platform-communications-with-transport-layer-security-certificates/configure-tls-certificates-for-inter-splunk-communication
vendor:          splunk-launch.conf [] SPLUNK_FIPS https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/splunk-launch.conf
vendor:          web.conf [settings] sslVersions https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/secure-splunk-platform-communications-with-transport-layer-security-certificates/configure-tls-protocol-version-support-for-secure-connections-between-splunk-platform-instances
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The FIPS 140-2 validated cryptographic module and the host kernel FIPS
                 state, which determine which algorithms actually exist to be selected
external:        FIPS mode is an install-time, one-way setting
                 (splunk-launch.conf.spec:110-130), so enabling it on a running instance is
                 a reinstall or upgrade rather than a configuration change
external:        SPLK-CL-000430 also names outputs.conf on forwarders and the OpenLDAP
                 client ldap.conf, which are configured on other hosts or outside Splunk's
                 conf layer
external:        SPLK-CL-000430 treats cipherSuite and ecdhCurves as compliant either when
                 absent, in which case the FIPS-mode cryptographic module selects the
                 algorithms, or when set to the exact lists its fix text names, so those
                 two settings are not asserted as conditions here

citation:        SPLK-CL-000390 fix text (SPLUNK_FIPS=1 and SPLUNK_COMMON_CRITERIA=1 before
                 first start) and SPLK-CL-000430 fix text (sslVersions = tls1.2,
                 sslVersionsForClient = tls1.2, with the note "Splunk Enterprise must
                 operate in FIPS mode to limit the algorithms allowed");
                 splunk-launch.conf.spec:110-130 (SPLUNK_FIPS vocabulary [0|1]);
                 server.conf.spec:765-779 and 780-795 (sslVersions and sslVersionsForClient
                 vocabulary ssl3, tls1.0, tls1.1, tls1.2, with "*" selecting all and "tls"
                 selecting tls1.0 or newer); web.conf.spec:239-250 (same vocabulary for
                 Splunk Web)
finding:         splunk-launch.conf does not set SPLUNK_FIPS = 1, or the TLS version
                 settings in server.conf [sslConfig] and web.conf [settings] are not pinned
                 to TLS 1.2, so the application does not confine hashing, key derivation
                 and signature operations to FIPS-validated algorithms.
